-6. Stop when the predicate is met. A plateau is not a stop, so keep going and pivot your approach to push past it. Surface a genuine dead end rather than spinning, and never relax the predicate to declare victory.
+6. Stop when the predicate is met, or when the time budget runs out. Within the budget a plateau is not a stop, so keep going and pivot your approach to push past it. Surface a genuine dead end rather than spinning, and never relax the predicate to declare victory. Cutting scope is different: drop the pitch's nice-to-haves in the open and report the cut. When the budget runs out, stop and report what passed and what is still unsolved. The unsolved part goes back to shaping.
 
 **Reply:** the exit condition, iterations run, what landed, what was discarded, final predicate state.
